WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:06.799
HBO has just put out a teaser trailer for
Game of Thrones Season 7 called Sigils.

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:11.599
The video touches on some important plot points
and conflicts from the story so far, while

00:00:11.599 --> 00:00:16.010
hinting at the broader themes we’ll see
in the seasons to come.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:21.190
It begins with a three-headed dragon, the
sigil of House Targaryen – the family of

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.230
Daenerys.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:28.810
We hear Dany talk about her father, the Mad
King Aerys who was notoriously crazy and cruel.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.300
One of the central conflicts of Daenerys’
character is the tension between her trying

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:39.460
to be a peaceful and compassionate ruler,
but also having a need for violence and vengeance,

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.680
fire and blood – some fans worry she’s
becoming like her father.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:50.110
We then see a stag, sigil of House Baratheon,
fighting the Targaryen dragon.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:54.399
This represents Robert’s Rebellion, the
war twenty years ago where Robert Baratheon

00:00:54.399 --> 00:00:58.420
defeated Aerys Targaryen and became the King
of Westeros.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:04.220
We hear Robert say he’ll kill every Targaryen
he gets his hands on, he hates them, partly

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:10.330
because Dany’s brother Prince Rhaegar ran
off with the woman Robert loved, Lyanna Stark

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:14.970
– who we saw in Season 6 giving birth to
Jon Snow.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:19.950
We might find out more about Jon’s parents
this next season.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:24.780
We then see a lion, sigil of House Lannister,
savaging a stag.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.670
This represents the death of King Robert,
which was brought about by Cersei and Lancel

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:30.760
Lannister.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:35.820
Also remember that Robert’s brothers Renly
and Stannis Baratheon were a thing for a while,

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:41.430
until Stannis was killed by Brienne, and Renly
killed by a shadowy vagina monster.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:46.400
So it’s been a rough couple a years for
the Baratheon family – though Robert’s

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.970
bastard Gendry is still out there.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:55.240
We see the head of a direwolf, sigil of House
Stark, and hear King Joffrey ordering the

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.790
execution of Lord Eddard.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:02.280
Things only get worse for the Starks from
there – with the deaths of Robb and Catelyn

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:07.170
at the Red Wedding, and the loss of Winterfell
to ironborn then Boltons…

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:12.640
In the books, there’s a huge complex conspiracy
to return the Starks to power – go watch

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:18.480
that video – but in the show Jon and Sansa
take back the north in a battle with the Boltons.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.450
Bran Stark, meanwhile, has become a psychic
tree-boy, Arya Stark has become a face-changing

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:28.590
Frey-slaying ninja assassin and Rickon Stark
has become a pincushion.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:32.640
We see the tentacles of the kraken of House
Greyjoy.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.390
King Balon Greyjoy tried to make to the Iron
Islands great again, but he was kind of an

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:42.580
idiot and failed, ended up killed by his brother
Euron, who now leads the ironborn towards

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:46.940
Dany, though Balon’s kids Yara and Theon
get there first.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:52.000
Euron is a seriously scary dude in the books
and there’s no doubt he’ll be a major

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.500
bad guy in Season 7 of Thrones.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:01.500
We then see a bear, sigil of House Mormont,
which is kind of odd, cause the Mormonts aren’t

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:06.540
a major house – they’re the family of
Lyanna, Maege, Jeor and Jorah.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:12.460
Jorah of course has that disease, greyscale,
and is currently out looking for a cure.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:18.760
Funnily enough, Sam Tarly has just arrived
at the Citadel, the university of Westeros.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:23.460
If anyone can heal Jorah, that’s where they’d
be.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:29.650
We see a lion’s paw tangled in the thorny
growths of a rose, sigil of House Tyrell.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:34.740
The Tyrells were involved in many plots to
gain power over the Lannisters, but ultimately

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:38.340
couldn’t scheme their way out of being blown
up by Cersei.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.230
Olenna still lives though, and she joins an
alliance with the Sand Snakes of Dorne and

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:47.310
Varys and Daenerys to fight against Cersei,
who crowns herself Queen of Westeros beside

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.569
her cronies Qyburn and the zombie-Mountain.

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:55.500
There’s a nice irony hearing Qyburn proclaiming
Cersei “Protector of the Seven Kingdoms”

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.530
when she’s done far more damage than good
to the realm.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:04.360
Cersei’s brother and lover Jaime might finally
question his relationship with her.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:08.800
Meanwhile the other brother Tyrion is on board
with Dany.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:14.209
We then get this wide, sweeping view of the
whole complex political clusterfuck that is

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:16.590
the last six seasons of Thrones.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:21.450
Daenerys speaks of “spokes on a wheel”
which alludes to the ultimate pointlessness

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:27.150
of these petty fights for power – the sigils
crack and crumble to dust and we zoom out

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:32.570
to show the “one war that matters”, the
real enemy, lookin like a blue-eyed Sauron

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:38.380
on the screen – the Others, the white walkers,
and their army of the dead marching from beyond

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:43.780
the Wall to destroy everyone – no matter
their sigil.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:49.030
There are just two short seasons left in Game
of Thrones, and shit is rapidly getting real.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:53.500
Once-separate plotlines are crashing together,
major characters are dropping like flies,

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:58.690
new revelations are solving old mysteries
– this seventh season of the show should

00:04:58.690 --> 00:04:59.950
be spectacular.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:04.780
We’ll speculate in more detail when more
trailers and stuff come out, but for now,

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:09.460
check out our other videos – there’re
summaries, detailed analyses of theories and

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:14.010
characters, and videos on every episode of
Thrones Season 6 – there will be a similar

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.000
series for Season 7.

